description:
Design a clock divider circuit that generates a slower clock signal from an input clock. The module takes an input clock signal (clk_in) and a reset signal. It counts clock cycles using a 25-bit counter that resets when it reaches a predefined value (12,500,000). Upon reaching this count, it toggles the output clock signal (clk_out) and resets the counter. The reset signal ensures that both the counter and the output clock are initialized to zero when activated. This effectively reduces the frequency of the input clock signal for use in lower frequency applications.
module top_module(
    input clk_in,
    input reset,
    output reg clk_out
);

code:
module top_module(
    input clk_in,
    input reset,
    output reg clk_out
);reg [24:0] counter;

always @(posedge clk_in or posedge reset) begin
    if (reset) begin
        counter <= 0;
        clk_out <= 0;
    end else begin
        counter <= counter + 1;
        if (counter == 12499999) begin
            counter <= 0;
            clk_out <= ~clk_out;
        end
    end
end

endmodule

