description:
Design a circuit that functions as a four-bit multiplier. It takes two 4-bit binary inputs, A and B, and computes their product, producing an 8-bit output. The multiplication is implemented using a combinatorial approach that iteratively calculates partial products for each bit of B, shifting and accumulating the results to generate the final output value.
module top_module(
  input [3:0] A,
  input [3:0] B,
  output reg [7:0] out // Changed from wire to reg
);

code:
module top_module(
  input [3:0] A,
  input [3:0] B,
  output reg [7:0] out // Changed from wire to reg
);reg [7:0] result;
  integer i;

  always @ (A or B) begin
    result = 0;
    for (i = 0; i < 4; i = i + 1) begin
      result = result + (B[i] * {A, 2'b0} << i);
    end
    out = result; // Now this assignment is valid
  end

endmodule

