description:
Design a 4-bit binary counter with a reset feature. The counter increments on each rising edge of the clock signal. If the reset input is asserted, the counter is initialized to zero. Once the counter reaches its maximum value of 15 (binary 1111), it wraps around and resets back to zero.
module top_module(
    q,
    clk,
    rst
);

code:
module top_module(
    q,
    clk,
    rst
);output reg [3:0] q;
    input clk;
    input rst;

    always @(posedge clk) begin
        if (rst) begin
            q <= 4'b0000;
        end else begin
            q <= q + 1;
            if (q == 4'b1111) begin
                q <= 4'b0000;
            end
        end
    end

endmodule

