Design a finite state machine (FSM) that processes a single input signal and produces an output based on its current state. The FSM transitions through several states (s0 to s4) when the input is low, but transitions to a terminal state (s5) under various conditions including when the input is high or upon reaching s4. The output is asserted high only when the FSM is in the s5 state, indicating a specific condition has been met based on the input sequence. The design is suitable for applications where state-dependent behavior is required, such as input validation or sequence detection.
